  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 308 AM CDT Sun Aug 30 2026\n\nToday...\n\nThe forecast continues to be on track with little change:\n\nAn upper-lvl high over the Southwest & Texas continues to \nexpand towards the Southeast. As the high progresses, heat indices \nare expected to hit triple digits this afternoon, with increased \nhumidity. A cut-off low will track westwards, bringing PoPs of 40-\n15% to our southeastern sites. This corridor of \nmoisture/precipitation will make its way northwards mid-week, which \nwill be elucidated on below.\n\nThis Week...\n\nThe aforementioned high will settle over the Southeast CONUS around \nTuesday, lingering through the rest of the week. Dangerous heat \nconcerns are expected to return as highs range in the mid/upper 90s \nand heat indices reach 105-110F. As such, a limited heat graphic \nwill be messaged today. As the high settles, additional cut-off low \ndisturbances will traverse around the ridge, bringing deep moisture \nand storm chances (25-50%) starting along the HWY 84 corridor. Mid-\nweek, rain chances will expand to the I-20 corridor and eastern MS \nas the pattern lingers and wavers northward into the end of the \nweek.",
